WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:04.120
Severity is useful, but it is not the same as real-world risk.

00:00:04.340 --> 00:00:07.460
Prioritization asks whether the component is affected,

00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:11.200
whether the condition is reachable or usable in the deployed workload,

00:00:11.420 --> 00:00:13.180
and what consequence would follow.

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:18.200
A critical label without deployment context may be less urgent than a lower-scored issue

00:00:18.420 --> 00:00:20.500
under active exploitation.

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:24.320
Increase urgency for known exploitation, internet exposure,

00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:29.500
reachable vulnerable functions, privileged workloads, sensitive data, critical services,

00:00:29.720 --> 00:00:32.920
weak compensating controls, or broad deployment.

00:00:33.140 --> 00:00:38.020
Consider the image's base ancestry because one fix may address many dependent workloads.

00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:40.000
Affected environment matters.

00:00:40.220 --> 00:00:44.940
A production image handling external traffic differs from a private development artifact

00:00:45.160 --> 00:00:46.760
that is never deployed.

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:51.620
Development findings still require ownership because old images can be promoted later,

00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:55.600
copied into another registry, or become part of a future release.

00:00:55.820 --> 00:01:00.060
Validate scanner evidence, distribution backports, package use,

00:01:00.280 --> 00:01:02.520
and fixed versions before assigning work.

00:01:02.740 --> 00:01:08.020
Document false positives and accepted mitigations so teams do not repeat the same analysis

00:01:08.240 --> 00:01:10.560
or quietly suppress a valid finding.

00:01:10.780 --> 00:01:14.620
Compensating controls can reduce likelihood or impact through segmentation,

00:01:14.840 --> 00:01:20.200
disabled features, restricted identity, runtime policy, or service isolation.

00:01:20.420 --> 00:01:24.980
They rarely remove the need to track the underlying vulnerability and should have

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:26.080
evidence,

00:01:26.300 --> 00:01:28.460
ownership, and review dates.

00:01:28.680 --> 00:01:33.160
Prioritization should produce an ordered remediation queue, target date, owner,

00:01:33.380 --> 00:01:35.140
and rationale.

00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:40.000
Reassess when exploitation intelligence, exposure, deployment,

00:01:40.220 --> 00:01:42.300
or business criticality changes.

00:01:42.520 --> 00:01:47.240
The purpose is to direct limited engineering capacity toward the greatest current risk

00:01:47.460 --> 00:01:49.940
while keeping every residual item visible.
